@startuml runtime_execution_result_read
title Read Committed Results for an Exact Execution Target
' Contract: pi-mono-java-design 2ee2a3211da68ad87b0d9cab353e691b00bdaebd
' Java baseline: 201d75ed; implementation sources: 0aa0cf8f and 1e9ab28c
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeExecutionResultRepository.java#readSegmentEvents
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeExecutionResultMapper.xml#listSegmentEvents and #findExecutionTerminal
' Pi baseline: 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3
' Pi source: packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts#runAgentLoop and #prepareToolCall
' Observed behavior: a confirming segment may later also link the actual execution terminal event.
' Design reason: a segment response must stop at its first idle while an interrupt waits for the actual terminal.
' Java divergence: shared database result segments are a CampusClaw architecture change.
start
:Receive the accepted exact Session, execution, root and segment identity;
if (Exact identity exists?) then (yes)
if (Read segment events?) then (yes)
  :Validate afterSeq >= 0 and limit > 0;
  :Read linked committed events in ascending sequence;
  :Keep afterSeq < eventSeq <= first segment terminal sequence;
  :Read the exact segment state;
  :Return batch and whether its first idle has been reached;
else (no)
  :Verify the requested segment belongs to the exact root execution;
  :Require execution state TERMINAL;
  :Read only the actual committed execution terminal event;
endif
else (no)
  :Return empty;
endif
stop
@enduml
